  "id": "information-processing-model",
  "term": "information-processing model",
  "definition": "In this source, the information-processing model is a way of understanding performance as a sequence in which a person takes in changing visual information, makes a decision, and then carries out an action. It is used to link training effects to stages of processing reflected in reaction time, decision-making accuracy, and motor control.",
